course: dictionary
lesson: 12703
title: Doggo: a cute dog or a hidden one
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word «doggo» has two meanings, and the context tells you which one you need. Online, a picture of a fluffy puppy with the words «What a good doggo!» means the dog is cute, so doggo is a playful word for a dog.
explain: «The fox lay doggo in the long grass until the hunters had gone.» Here doggo has nothing to do with a dog. To lie doggo means to keep still and quiet so nobody finds you. Ask yourself: is this sentence about an animal, or about hiding?
explain: Doggo is slang, so it is informal. The tone is jokey and playful, and in old stories it can be secretive. Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence: does «lay quiet and hidden» still make sense? If it does, you have found the right meaning.
fact: Doggo is slang: an informal word that people use in casual speech and online.
fact: As a noun, «doggo» means a dog, said in a cute, playful way.
fact: «Lie doggo» means to stay hidden and quiet, not moving, so you are not found.
fact: «Lie doggo» is old UK and Australian slang, so you will mostly meet it in older stories.
fact: Doggo often appears in dog memes next to «pupper» and «heckin», which are playful words too.
exercise: «What a good doggo!» What does doggo mean here? | *A dog, said in a cute, playful way | A hiding place under the stairs | A slow, sleepy cat | A type of bread
exercise: «The thief lay doggo behind the wall until the guards passed.» What does lay doggo mean? | To run as fast as you can | *To stay hidden and quiet so you are not found | To sleep in a warm bed | To dig a hole in the garden
exercise: Which sentence uses doggo to mean a dog? | «We had to doggo the homework before tea.» | *«The doggo wagged its tail at everyone in the park.» | «We lay doggo in the tent so the teacher would not find us.» | «It was doggo weather, so we stayed indoors.»
test: «The little doggo rolled over for a belly rub.» What does doggo mean here? | A type of bread | A slow, sleepy cat | A hiding place under the stairs | *A dog, said in a cute way
test: «Sam decided to lie doggo until the bell rang.» What does lie doggo mean? | To shout for help | *To hide quietly and not move | To jump up and down | To eat a big lunch
exam: Read this: «Mum said, "Those videos of a fluffy doggo always make me smile."» Why is doggo a jokey word here? | *Because it is a playful, cute word for a dog | Because it is a number | Because it means a secret hiding place | Because it is a formal word from a law book
